<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kanva dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">73 BCE – 28 BCE (approx.) · capital Pataliputra</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Brahmin dynasty of four kings that ruled Magadha after the Shungas, in the twilight of Pataliputra's ancient power.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 73 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasudeva-kanva">Vasudeva Kanva</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> minister of the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shunga-empire">Shunga</a> king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devabhuti">Devabhuti</a>, had his master killed and took the throne. The Kanvas inherited a shrunken kingdom in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a> and the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pataliputra">Pataliputra</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty is known almost entirely from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a>, which list four kings, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasudeva-kanva">Vasudeva</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhumimitra">Bhumimitra</a>, Narayana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susharman">Susharman</a>, ruling for a total of 45 years. Coins bearing the name Bhumimitra may belong to the second king. Nothing reliable is known of their government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susharman">Susharman</a> was killed around 28 BCE by a king of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/satavahana-dynasty">Andhras</a>, usually taken to be a ruler of the Satavahana dynasty. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a> then broke into small local principalities until the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> revived it in the 4th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kanva-dynasty.jpg" alt="Kanva dynasty" width="320" height="302"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lessman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_in_50_bc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>73 BCE – 28 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pataliputra</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vasudeva Kanva, Susharman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vedic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Prakrit, Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kanvas, Kanvayana dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-50&amp;focus=kanva-dynasty" aria-label="Kanva dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6933 1236 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kanva dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7253 1492L7253 1492M7253 1492L7165 1820"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7253 1492h0M7165 1820h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7253 1492h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7253 1492h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pataliputra. <a href="/atlas?year=-50&amp;focus=kanva-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
